 "title": "Assessor | Benton County",
 "text": "-->\nAssessor | Benton County\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nBENTON COUNTY\nAbout\nWelcome\nCommunity\nDepartments\nContact\nBusiness Info\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nCounty Government\nAll Departments\nAssessor\nOur primary goal is to perform uniform, equalized, and fair assessments to all taxpayers.\nOther Assessor duties are as follows:\n Serves as secretary for the County Property Tax Assessment Board of Appeals (PTABOA)\n Reviews and addresses all aspects of property appeals\n Oversees the general reassessment process\n Maintain Not-for Profit Exemptions and Sales Disclosures\n Notify taxpayers of yearly assessment changes by providing a Notice of Assessment (Form 11)\nWe encourage taxpayers to ask questions regarding their assessments.\nMY TAXES ARE TOO HIGH NOW WHAT\nThere are many aspects that go into a tax bill, understanding them is helpful to determine what has changed.\nDid my assessment go up? Why and what can I do?\nIndiana Assessments are based on market value in use. So, when you get your form 11 (notice of assessment) from the assessor’s office, look at it. Is the value stated what you think you can reasonably sell your property for in the market? If not, then file an appeal form 130 with the County Assessor. These forms are available online at www.dlgf.gov or in the Assessor’s office. You can also file an appeal at http://beacon.schneidercorp.com .\nIf your assessment is reasonably close to your marketable value, I would then check my deductions and be sure you currently have all possible.\nFor more helpful information please see our Assessment Fact Sheet .\nPERSONAL PROPERTY INFORMATION\nThe assessment date for Personal Property is January 1 st of every year. Filing due date is May 15 . Only if you have acquisition costs of $2,000,000 and over\nParcel Information\nTaxpayers can access parcel and assessment information through our GIS.\nhttps://beacon.schneidercorp.com/\nlowtaxinfo.com\nLOCATION\n706 E 5th Street; Suite 23 Fowler, IN 47944\nBenton County Courthouse\n(2nd Floor)\nHOURS\nMonday - Friday\n8:30 am to 4:00 pm EST\nClosed on major holidays\nCONTACT\nPH: 765-884-1205\nFax: 765-884-2074\nADDITIONAL LINKS\nAgricultural Land Assessments\nhttps://www.in.gov/dlgf/assessments/agricultural-land-assessments/\nInterested in learning more about property taxes and how they are figured? Watch Purdue Extension Local Government YouTube channel for informative videos by Larry DeBoer and Tamara Ogle here\nRead Larry DeBoers column, Capital Comments, where he also writes about state and local government policy here .\nADDITIONAL DOCUMENTS\nApplications, Permits, and Zoning\nSales Disclosure\nhttps://www.in.gov/dlgf/assessments/sales-disclosure-form-information/\nExemptions\nhttps://www.in.gov/dlgf/assessments/exemptions/\nSTAFF\nKelly Balensiefer, Assessor\nassessor@bentoncounty.in.gov\nTOWNSHIP TRUSTEES\nAll Departments\nBENTON COUNTY COURTHOUSE\n706 E 5th Street\nFowler, IN 47944\nHours of Operation\nGENERAL NAVIGATION\nAbout\n​\nContact\n​\nCovid-19 Updates\n​\nEducation / Schools\n​\nGovernment\n​\nHistory\n​\nHome\n​\nJob Openings\n​\nPermits\n​\nUtilities\n​\nVoting Information\n​\nWelcome\n​\nCarbon Sequestration\nCOMMUNITY RESOURCES\nSee Also Community Departments\nADA & Title VI Resources\nLocal Experiences\nBusiness Directory\nEvents\n​\nHealth Department\n​\nLibraries\n​\nVeterans Affairs\nDEPARTMENTS\nAdministration\nAssessor​\nAuditor​\n​\nCentral Committees\n​\nCounty Clerk​\n​\nCommissioners​\n​\nCounty Council​\n​\nRecorder​\n​\nTreasurer\nCommunity\n​\nADA & Title VI Resources\nChamber of Commerce\n​\nBe In Benton\n​\nCooperative Extension Service ​\n​\nEconomic Development Department\n​\nBenton County Tourism\n​\nFamily & Children Division\n​\nRetirement Village\n​\nVeterans Affairs\nDEPARTMENTS\nHealth & Safety\n​\nDispatch - 911\n​\nEmergency Medical Services (EMS​)\n​\nHealth Department\n​\nHomeland Security &\nEmergency Mgt.​\n​\nSheriff's Department\n& Jail\nInfrastructure\n​\nAdvisory Plan\nCommission\nBuilding Inspector​\n​\nHighway Department\n​\nSoil / Water Conservation\n​\nSurveyor\nJustice\nCircuit Court\nProbation\nProsecuting Attorney\nOUR COMMUNITIES\nTown of Ambia\n​\nTown of Boswell\n​\nTown of Earl Park\n​\nTown of Fowler\n​\nTown of Otterbein\n​\nTown of Oxford\nHELPFUL LINKS\nSmart911 SignUp & LogIn\n​\nGIS Mapping: For property aerial maps, parcel assessment, and tax info.\n​\n2021 Indiana Municipal Guide\n​\nGuide to Securing your Home\n​\nVoter Information\n​\nIndiana Voter Portal\n​\nIndiana Office of Energy Development\n​\n2018 Benton County Comprehensive Plan\n​\nBest Colleges in Indiana 2022\n2025 Benton County Indiana All Rights Reserved\nWebmaster: Signature Web Creations\nbottom of page",
